[[:db/retract 17592186115442 :activity/steps 17592186116386] [:db/retract 17592186115442 :activity/steps 17592186116388] [:db/retract 17592186115442 :activity/steps 17592186115996] [:db/retract 17592186116386 :step/next 17592186115996] [:db/retract 17592186115996 :step/next 17592186116387] [:db/retract 17592186116388 :step/next 17592186116389] {:db/id 17592186115405 :knowledge-point/title "Solving Multi-Step Problems Involving Complementary Angles" :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186114981 :question/math-academy-id "e-18993" :question/problem "In the figure below, $\\angle AOC$ and $\\angle COB$ are complementary angles. If $\\angle AOC \\cong \\angle BOD$ and $m \\angle COB = 50^\\circ,$ find $m \\angle AOD.$\n\n![](images/60/60c48e8ce5fd289f6aa7b80cfd5a99db1adf9a0603e6162c1fb5b4dcf1a7e15d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\angle AOC$ and $\\angle COB$ are complementary angles, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOC+m∠COB & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠AOC+{50}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ m∠AOC & ={40}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $\\angle AOC \\cong \\angle BOD,$ we have\n\n$$\nm \\angle BOD = m \\angle AOC=40^\\circ .\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AOD & =m∠AOC+m∠COB+m∠BOD \\\\  & ={40}^{∘}+{50}^{∘}+{40}^{∘} \\\\  & ={130}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116445 :tutorial/math-academy-id 13548 :tutorial/content "**Complementary angles** are two angles whose measures have a sum of $90^\\circ,$ a right angle.\n\n![](images/27/2723049c087f5fa7b061bc9f1d4fb8c894c1e94aee3dfb994a237cd889a377e0.png)\n\nFor example, the angles in the diagram above are complementary because the sum of their measures is $90^\\circ\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n60^\\circ +30^\\circ = 90^\\circ\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id "tutorial-62b39d73-2c91-59ba-9e98-44a61a98c7b4" :tutorial/id #uuid "62b39d73-2c91-59ba-9e98-44a61a98c7b4" :tutorial/math-academy-id 15157 :tutorial/title "Working With Diagrams" :tutorial/content "Now, consider the following diagram.\n\n![](images/02/02d8744bbc39ac9ed10d276071599f9008185023ebdfc3aaf97aebd498d82629.png)\n\nLet's solve for $x$ given the figure above.\n\nFrom the diagram, we have two complementary angles, so\n\n$$\n46^\\circ + (8x + 4^\\circ) = 90^\\circ.\n$$\n\nHence, we can solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{46}^{∘}+(8x+{4}^{∘}) & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 8x+{50}^{∘} & ={90}^{∘} \\\\ 8x & ={40}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={5}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115442 :activity/steps ["step-fab99fb7-13ba-526e-9805-8357cfddf511" "step-70f7bf88-80a0-59ab-b3a1-742cf3923640"] :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116385 :step/math-academy-id 484813 :step/next "step-fab99fb7-13ba-526e-9805-8357cfddf511" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-fab99fb7-13ba-526e-9805-8357cfddf511" :step/id #uuid "fab99fb7-13ba-526e-9805-8357cfddf511" :step/content 17592186503647 :step/math-academy-id 484814 :step/next "step-70f7bf88-80a0-59ab-b3a1-742cf3923640" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-70f7bf88-80a0-59ab-b3a1-742cf3923640" :step/id #uuid "70f7bf88-80a0-59ab-b3a1-742cf3923640" :step/content "tutorial-62b39d73-2c91-59ba-9e98-44a61a98c7b4" :step/math-academy-id 619142 :step/next 17592186116387 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116387 :step/math-academy-id 484817 :step/next 17592186116389 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186116389 :step/math-academy-id 484820 :db/ensure [:step/validate]}]
